<title>USA: Japan priority must be strong domestic demand - US.</title>
<headline>Japan priority must be strong domestic demand - US.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's economic priority should be the maintenance of strong domestic demand, U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We've been advising the Japanese that their priority has to be maintaining strong domestic demand,&quot; he told CNBC television.</p>
<p>&quot;That continues to be our priority for the months and years ahead,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
